WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
Touch an old-fashioned filament
bulb that has been on for a

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.690
while, and it could burn your fingers.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.770
An L E D bulb giving out the
same light is far cooler.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.250
To make the same light,

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.790
the filament bulb needs far
more energy every second.

6
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.790
But energy is never destroyed.

7
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.430
So where does all the filament
bulb's extra energy go?

8
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.870
In this mission, you'll follow
the energy as a device does its

9
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.050
job, and separate the
useful part from the rest.

10
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.590
You'll calculate efficiency,

11
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.550
and compare how well different
devices use the energy they are

12
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.610
given.

13
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.860
Your mission: track down the
filament bulb's extra energy.
